    "result_text": "Done. Full suite is green (25 tests, 0 failures).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `membershipTier` is a computed, read-only field derived from an owner's existing state, so I implemented it the same way as the sibling fields `membershipNumber`, `displayName`, and `initials` \u2014 as an OpenAPI schema property plus a MapStruct expression. No new OfficeFloor endpoint was needed since this rides on the existing owner response mapping.\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `membershipTier` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` expression:\n   ```java\n   (namesakeCount != null && namesakeCount == 0 && email != null && !email.isBlank()) ? \"SILVER\" : \"BRONZE\"\n   ```\n\nThis yields `SILVER` when `namesakeCount` is 0 and an email is present, and `BRONZE` otherwise \u2014 matching the spec. `Cp15Tests` (both cases) and the related `Cp13Tests` (namesakeCount) pass, along with the rest of the suite.",
